# Canonical commit identity for this repository.
#
# Commits were made from several machines with differing git configs. This maps
# every stray name/address onto one identity so `git log`, `git shortlog` and
# `git blame` show a single author.
#
# Note: this is presentation only. It does not rewrite history, and GitHub's web
# UI ignores .mailmap — the original addresses remain in the commit objects.
# Preventing new ones is a matter of `git config` on each machine.

